{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821345-how-important-has-the-resources-background-been-in-your-in-your-chronicles","id":821345,"title":"How important has the Resources background been in your in your chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-01T18:20:52-08:00","id":821345,"title":"How important has the Resources background been in your in your chronicles","content":"Just like the title I'm looking for examples of how people have used their resources backgrounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T18:43:59-08:00","id":821356,"title":"","content":"This may not be very helpful, but in my games (the ones I've run) Resources has only been important relative to the specific circumstance of a given instance: if the PCs needed money to get to another state/country/part of the world and nobody had more than 1 or 2 dots in Resources, then they had a problem. If they had 3+, then not so much. That's the general vibe I've experienced in games where I was a player, too -- it was only a piece of the puzzle, as it were, with its own advantages and drawbacks (money lets you do a lot of things most people can't/never will, but then it just as often comes with attachments and liabilities, too, that complicate things).<br /> <br /> I guess throw my &quot;view&quot; in with the &quot;it's just a part of things -- not more so, not less so, but a part&quot;-vote....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T02:10:31-08:00","id":821507,"title":"","content":"Resources are one of those things that are deeply context dependant, and that really depend on the character who wants to use them. It's a highly useful thing as a refernce to know what kind of expenses a character can make casually.<br /> <br /> I think my favourite use of Resources was with a &quot;Proffesional Facilitator&quot;. This was an Ananasi with Contacts 5 and Resources 5 that made sure that could be employed to get whatever your heart desired, no questions asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:33:02-08:00","id":821718,"title":"","content":"Not very for the most part, though one fellow player's character got a ten figure commission for recruiting a multi billionaire with a massive pharmaceutical empire into his clan at the end of a storyline. He'd previously had enough money to do pretty much whatever he wanted in that arena, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:22:59-08:00","id":822485,"title":"","content":"SNIP, delete this post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T13:55:44-08:00","id":822714,"title":"","content":"Depends a lot on the game in question. Werewolf rarely has Resources matter much, because most Garou operate outside of normal human society. Most of the games fall in the middle as PCs interact with human society on some level, but can have enough support from their various secret societies that most don't need Resources much. Hunter is definitely the game where you feel it the most, because the Imbued only have what they can personally obtain; no elders to give them access to anything, or help out with extra perks.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with making Resources matter, is that you really only need one PC to have it if the PCs are generally cooperative. One PC with Resource 4 or 5 can easily care for the rest of the group in terms of housing, food, transportation, and other supplies unless you purposefully make plot relevant stuff really expensive.<br /> <br /> A lot of the later ST systems have done a bit more to give Resources mechanical weight, which seems to help increase its importance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T07:39:35-08:00","id":823335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/821345-how-important-has-the-resources-background-been-in-your-in-your-chronicles?p=822714#post822714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the later ST systems have done a bit more to give Resources mechanical weight, which seems to help increase its importance.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:05:14-08:00","id":823584,"title":"","content":"I'll use CofD as an example, simply because people can download the GMCRU for free to reference if they don't have any of the books:<br /> <br /> In CofD there's an Availability system where equipment, services, etc. all get an Availability rating from 1-5 (assuming they don't get an N/A for &quot;not for sale&quot;).<br /> <br /> Since Resources directly interacts with the Availability system, it can help eliminate the, &quot;One PC has Resources 5, we don't have to worry about money any more,&quot; of a more loose system. Since you know what X Resources can practically get you, the importance of Resources goes up as groups are going to want to make sure they're not overtaxing what Resources can get them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:31:51-08:00","id":823607,"title":"","content":"A related Question? Why are their ANY Poor Supernaturals in existence unless their poor by choice.<br /> <br /> A changeling with chincancery or legerdiman can become a master thief... with soothsay he can bless himself or a puppet... Mages can either use entrop to bless themselves or use matter to create gold..vampires with obfuscate make master thieves, garou can work well enough as I allready suggested in Bounty hunting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:22:58-08:00","id":823771,"title":"","content":"Why are there poor supernaturals besides ample good reasons via choice?<br /> <br /> 1) The effort of hiding what they are to maintain work among humans, combined with the efforts in their supernatural life, makes it too big of a pain. This is especially true for groups like Nosferatu, Metis, and so on where part of their nature includes obvious physical issues. <br /> 2) Most supernatural powers are not 100% reliable/other drawbacks. Relying on powers to make a living increases the odds that they fail at a significantly inconvenient time, and your whole operation becomes at risk.<br /> 3) Both mortal and supernatural forces operating at institutional levels beyond the scope of individual powers to control are actively pushing back. Making yourself extra lucky at the casinos is going to get the pit-bosses suspicious of you, and if you continue to power yourself past that, eventually it'll ping the radar of a supernatural that's going to be pisses at you for this and is probably more powerful than you.<br /> 4) I think there's a lot of assumptions about how easy it is to profit off of crime on a small scale. You can't just be a &quot;master thief,&quot; via super-sneaking. Being able to steal things doesn't leave you rolling in cash. You need to have a way to fence what you steal. You need to have a way of hiding the tracks so that the illegally sold items can't be traced back to you. All that takes time, effort, and generally money. It takes partners, all of whom are potential liabilities because they knew about you. The more something is worth, the harder it is to get paid for cleanly. Having half a million dollars in rare paintings hidden in your home is worthless if you can't sell them, or put them up as collateral for loans, because that means getting caught.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T18:31:08-08:00","id":823909,"title":"","content":"I agree with Just John, resources are only important in so far as to how the players leverage them. I've had people play vagrants and be just as successful in game as someone playing resources 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:52:48-08:00","id":824059,"title":"","content":"The issue with resources conceptually is that it is in principal not very hard to break the minds of some extremely wealthy mortals with some combination of Blood Bonding, Presence, and Dominate, and thereby readily acquire arbitrary amounts of resources if you are sufficiently motivated and ambitious. Obviously this may displease other vampires with stakes in such creatures, but it's not like every would-be plutocrat and heir is accounted for. Using Dominate, Auspex, etc. to acquire the information necessary to steal or reallocate vast amounts of wealth is also viable, and Dominate and Obfuscate provide plenty of opportunities for covering your tracks as need be. In principal, with a decent Finance and Intelligence/Wits any Kindred should be able to work out a way to get rich quick based on blood bonding alone- the main problem is that there are many things in the WoD that can't be brute forced with finances (or which will be met with comparable largesse by the similarly if not more loaded Elders etc. whom you are competing against). You can only equip and mobilize private armies so discreetly, after all.<br /> <br /> If memory serves Gilded Cage or Midnight Siege claimed in context of redistributing wealth that the above techniques can't &quot;force people to go against their nature&quot;- but as with much of WW's attempt to establish the limitations of vampire powers in respect to mortals, this really doesn't make any sense (people spend vast sums on inane things or foolish trysts all the time- you're telling me the profligate or idle rich man isn't going to blow his fortune on someone he has become utterly devoted to and obsessed with?). Very few people are going to have &quot;frugality&quot; so utterly welded to their core nature that Presence 3 or a full blood bond won't have the ability to override their inhibitions to a significant extent (or just good old fashioned seduction mediated by Obfuscate or Presence). In principal a Tremere with Conjuration 3 can just conjure permanent stacks of money or priceless valuables so long as he has the blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> Demons and Magi can probably achieve comparable success in usurping the wills of the wealthy if they have invested their supernatural gimmicks appropriately (I'm not sure if Werewolves are especially suited to it, but I'm also not sure if it really matters. Worst comes to worst you can attempt a Delirium-cloaked bank robbery).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 02-05-2016, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T00:46:19-08:00","id":824089,"title":"","content":"Delirium-cloaked bank robbery would be grounds for harsh punishments as it breaks one of the key laws of the Garou.<br /> <br /> It comes down to the fact that just like people in normal life can become filthy rich if they put their minds to it, the same applies to the supernaturals. Some of them have morals, others lack the opportunity, yet others lack the competence. It's quite telling that the groups with stronger recruitment policies towards inventive and socially capable people tend to be the rich ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:10:36-08:00","id":825240,"title":"","content":"I'd think vampires would have a natural advantage in accruing material wealth in that they're immortal by default and have multiple lifetimes to build their fortunes. Might not affect neonate vampires so much, but anyone over a century old should be rolling in it unless they're specifically devoted to a monastic or nomadic existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T02:05:14-08:00","id":825324,"title":"","content":"Well, except the issues with trying to keep that money without revealing your immortal.<br /> <br /> If you're going Scrooge McDuck with a giant vault, you're going to get robbed as that grows because you can't really hide that much actual physical wealth. And all the people eyeing your stash are eventually going to notice the immortality thing (let alone all the other vampire parts).<br /> <br /> If you're investing the money to have it grow, you now have to repeatedly fake your death, and establish a new identity that people will believe isn't the previous you. And there's estate taxes and/or gift taxes that will become an issue.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is one of the reasons vampires don't operate solo. It's a lot easier to do these sorts of things if you're a Giovanni and there are actual families for the money to flow to new generations of while it accumulates. But that also spreads the money around between more people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T02:13:14-08:00","id":825325,"title":"","content":"Your innate abilities to enslave, mindwipe, or break the wills of people should facilitate the upkeep of successive false identities (maintained in their concealment by suborned bankers and regulatory officials- also great facilitation of money laundering in general) over the ages- not to mention that you can simply stash parts of your investments, finances, etc. under various ghouled or Conditioning-broken pawns. Obfuscate 3 and Vicissitude also allow for ready wholesale swapping of identities; Dominate coupled with judicious ghouling or Presence can also allow you to massage in memories or records of new identities that happen to resemble a distant 'ancestor'. Send it all out in 'inheritances' and 'bequests' (to your mewling puppets) and reel what you want back in to a suitable proxy or new identity at your convenience. Obviously this procedure does create points and times of vulnerability in respect to other Kindred meddling in your affairs- but there's not a lot of value that's without that kind of risk in Kindred society anyway. Getting yourself declared dead by a personal doctor (who can also be broken to your will if need be) is not especially challenging when you don't have vital signs to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 02-07-2016, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T03:30:26-08:00","id":825339,"title":"","content":"You realize how much of that doesn't work because of daylight? Unless your vampire is literally going around mind-whammying bank employees at night after tracking down where they all live (and not just their local branch, since they're going to need to also go after all the corporate head office folks who have the jobs of monitor activity to make sure this sort of thing doesn't happen).<br /> <br /> It's also a somewhat spurious base premise that amounts to, &quot;this is simple because vampires get 500 XP upon Embrace that they can spend ignoring any Discipline learning restrictions, need for justification/teachers, or Generation caps.&quot; Since we're talking multiple Disciplines at 3+ levels, all of the Attributes and Abilities at maxed out levels to ensure maximum reliability, and assuming that they never fail/botch these rolls, and their servants are perfect automatons (despite the books repeated warnings about how dangerous that is to count on) that don't ever decide to ruin the financial schemes by getting taken in by someone like Bernie Madoff thinking they were going to make their master so happy by increasing your wealth even more.<br /> <br /> Of course it seems simple if your character has a so many stats that money is practically pointless to them anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T03:38:13-08:00","id":825343,"title":"","content":"You don't need all of them, you just need some appropriate combination depending on your starting state and strategy. You certainly don't need elder level disciplines. A starting character can have six dots of disciplines if he caps out on flaws (five if he doesn't), so it's not unreasonable to expect an ancillae with a sufficiently strong interest in long-term wealth maintenance to have a pretty robust set of relevant faculties. No plan like this is without potential for diverse complications , but who says you're actually going to keep your ghouls and dominate-battered pawns around forever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T12:18:36-08:00","id":825520,"title":"","content":"Your argument for the &quot;ease&quot; of doing it is still basically assuming an extremely idealized situation where everything goes as planned at every step.<br /> <br /> Even on the mechanical angle,&quot;You can start with 6 dots in Disciplines,&quot; doesn't mean you're any good at them. This inherently have capped all your Abilities at 3, you'll need at least 3-4 Attributes at decent levels that you can't buff up like physicals with blood. So your dice-pools are going to all require lots of time and energy devoted to training before you can pull anything like this off with any solid trust in your powers to pull smooth things out. You also have no Merits, whatever Flaw penalties, you're stuck at starting levels for a bunch of important Advantages, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:32:37-08:00","id":826662,"title":"","content":"Most of the Human population has willpower 2-4, and if you're using temp willpower rather than permanent for dominate difficulties and the like, then difficulties are often going to be slightly lower than that (in that some % of people have expended some % of their mental energy some % of the time). Dominate and Entrancement difficulties against most of the links in the chain you'd want to suborn are going to be sufficiently low that you actually won't need especially large dice pools to get consistent results (and for the exceptionally strong willed, there's always your own WP points or more creative and involved approaches). Moreover, you don't need to start with six dots in social disciplines to be able to put mortals readily under your thumb, and the case we were talking about (a prosperous vampire sustaining wealth well beyond his reasonably expected lifespan) is likely to apply to Kindred who have some degree of additional experience beyond that of a default starting character. Many of the pathways proposed above are redundant with one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:34:30-08:00","id":826926,"title":"","content":"I would imagine that a character's Resources rating doesn't necessarily mean money and property that's legally in that character's name and has to be managed in person, any more than an Influence rating means that one is an elected official subject to publicity and oversight. What matters is that you have control over how it's spent, be that by doing an electronic transfer from a Swiss bank account, putting an issue to a vote in the board meeting of a company that you've been controlling from behind the scenes for generations, or having a lackey trade a brick of blood-infused cocaine for the crates of automatic weapons you want to buy in a meeting of speedboats off the Florida Keys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:24:15-07:00","id":875250,"title":"","content":"In most of the stories i ST'ed resources rarely mattered more than &quot;can i buy this or that vehicle, gun' and such, and very few Pcs ever bothered with a 3 or higher rating. They just stole what was needed at the time.. As a player, i have had over the years maybe 3 pcs who had 3 or even 4 in resources, and 2 of those were darkages viking (bruja/gangrel), and the other a glass walker homid..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T08:43:11-07:00","id":881010,"title":"","content":"For vampires, especially those of the social clans, accumulating resources can be the drive of the game. Living well is a nice thing for the character. Also you might need that comfortable living to spend time in research or whatnot. I really like to start the game with nothing and build backrounds up through rollplay. <br /> <br /> Furthermore<br /> High resources allows you to maintain other backrounds. your bribes keep the contacts and allies, your payments give you a private helicopter and a security force for your impregnable haven of high class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 05-03-2016, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}